          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#relation_to_the_initial_topos Relation to the initial topos
          %p
            One of the first applications of the Freyd cover was to deduce facts about the initial topos (initial with respect to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/logical+morphism"} logical morphisms
            — also called the
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+topos"} free topos
          .num_lemma
            %h6#lemma Lemma
            %p
              For any category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              with a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{1}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi C
                      %mo ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat{C}
              is
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small-projective"} small-projective
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo =
                    %mover
